  "all_ingredients_flat": "White peas, Onions, Ginger Garlic Paste, Green chili, Himalayan salt, Turmeric powder, Red chilli powder, Garam Masala Powder, Hing (asafetida), Tamarind paste, Date sugar, Cilantro, Pomegranate, Green Chutney",
  "instructions": "WHITE PEAS: Soak white peas overnight. Pressure cook them in the Instant Pot for 15-20 minutes. Mash 3-4 Tbsp cooked peas in a bowl & set them aside. I drained the peas out and used the Instant Pot for saut\u00e9ing the masala as well.\nMASALA: Set Instant Pot to saut\u00e9 mode. Dry saut\u00e9 onions & green chili until onion turn translucent. I add some water to keep the onions from sticking to the bottom. Then add Ginger Garlic paste & cook for 1 minute. Then add hing, red chili powder, turmeric powder, Garam Masala Powder & 1 Tbsp water. Cook for 2-3 minutes.\nCombine cooked peas, mashed peas, date sugar, tamarind paste & Himalayan salt [optional, to taste].Adjust the quantity of water. Bring to a boil, then cook for 7-10 minutes on low flame. Do a taste check & add more Garam Masala powder or red chili powder, if needed.\nGarnish with chopped cilantro, pomegranate & Green Chutney!",
  "cooking_methods": [
    "pressure cook",
    "saute",
    "boil",
    "no-cook"
  ],
  "serving_suggestion": "Garnish with chopped cilantro, pomegranate & Green Chutney!",
  "notes": "A recipe with BEANS (white peas), RAINBOW VEGGIES (onion), FRUITS (pomegranate), SWEETENER (date sugar), HERBS & SPICES (various). Himalayan salt [optional, to taste]. Adjust quantity of water. Add more Garam Masala powder or red chili powder, if needed. Add some water to keep onions from sticking to the bottom.",
